# 44. What I think is the most important thing to understand from this section

Don't read this article merely as:

> "Lucy Guo raised $40 million for an app where influencers can charge fans."

That's the surface-level interpretation.

The deeper story is:

> **Who owns the economic relationship between a creator and their audience?**

TikTok thinks it does.

Instagram thinks it does.

YouTube thinks it does.

Patreon thinks it can facilitate it.

Passes is betting that creators want to take more of that relationship for themselves.

And that's why investors from technology, entertainment, fashion and media are interested.

If Passes succeeds, it isn't merely another Patreon clone.

It could become **financial and operational infrastructure for internet personalities**.

That is the much larger opportunity the article is describing.

