Absolutely. I went back to the surviving HackMIT records and Lucy’s own later description, and we can reconstruct the weekend **much more concretely than I initially could**.

One caveat up front: there is **no surviving minute-by-minute diary, GitHub repository, or recording of the team’s conversations**, so I’ll distinguish between **documented facts** and **reasonable reconstruction/inference**. I don't want to turn an inference into a fake fact.

