# There's one chronology issue we need to be careful about

You asked earlier whether the 2014 interview/application material was written specifically to get accepted into Thiel.

The new evidence makes this more nuanced.

The **Thiel Fellowship application was due December 31, 2013**, so EduGames from February 2014 obviously **couldn't have been the project she submitted in that original application**.

But it could have influenced what she subsequently developed as her fellowship project.

So:

### Before application deadline

June 2013 — Google Hack for Change
July 2013 — LinkedIn HackDay
September 2013 — PennApps X / Codify
October 2013 — HackMIT / Nommit

### After application deadline

January 2014 — MHacks / Spontaneity
February 2014 — PennApps / EduGames

And she became a Thiel Fellow in 2014.

That's an important distinction.

