# What she apparently proposed to Thiel

The Thiel announcement gives us the clearest contemporary description:

**Goal:** make studying fun.

**Mechanism:** multiplayer educational games.

**Platform:** something that would allow students to study their normal schoolwork through games.

Then the later reporting adds:

**Customizable content.**

The teacher/educator could potentially adapt the game to whatever curriculum they were teaching. ([Women 2.0][5])

So conceptually:

```text
Traditional education

Teacher
   ↓
Curriculum
   ↓
Textbook / worksheet
   ↓
Student memorizes material
```

Lucy wanted:

```text
Teacher
   ↓
Curriculum
   ↓
CUSTOM GAME
   ↓
Students play together
   ↓
Learning happens through interaction
```

That's the central idea.

