Yes — and the new evidence changes one important part of the picture. I want to correct something from my previous answer before building the timeline:

**The 5.99% figure was accurate for the 2023–2024 period, but it is no longer her current percentage. Forbes now says Lucy owns roughly 3% of Scale.** The difference is largely explained by dilution from later financing and the 2025 Meta transaction. Forbes also says Scale paid shareholders a large dividend as part of that transaction. ([Forbes][1])

